course: dictionary
lesson: 8165
title: Reshape: change the shape, or change how things work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To reshape something means to change its shape, like pressing soft clay into a new form. It can also mean to change how something is organised or how it works, often in a big way.
explain: «When words travel into another language they are reshaped to fit its sounds.» The clue is the word "fit": borrowed words are changed so they can be said in the new language. Try your meaning in the sentence: "they are changed to fit its sounds" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Look at the example about Hawaiian. It has no r, s or t, and its syllables end in vowels, so «Merry Christmas» became «Mele Kalikimaka». Shape is the word hiding inside reshape, and it helps you guess that the word is about form, but the sentence shows the wider meaning too.
fact: To reshape means to change the shape of something, or to change how it is organised or works.
fact: Reshape is a verb: reshape, reshapes, reshaped, reshaping.
fact: In maths, you can cut and move the parts of a shape to reshape it, and its area stays the same.
fact: Words borrowed from one language are reshaped to fit the sounds of the new language: «Merry Christmas» became «Mele Kalikimaka» in Hawaiian.
fact: Japanese adds vowels too, so «ice cream» became «aisukurīmu».
exercise: «When words travel into another language they are reshaped to fit its sounds.» What does reshaped mean here? | *Changed to fit the new language's sounds | Forgotten | Copied exactly, letter for letter | Translated word for word into English
exercise: In maths, you reshape a shape by cutting and moving its parts. What stays the same? | The colour of the pencil | The number of corners | *The area | Nothing at all, everything is different
exercise: The new railway will ___ the town and how people move around it. Which word fits? | whisper | *reshape | drooped | famished
test: The invention began to reshape how people travel. What does reshape mean? | Make a small, quiet mark | Paint the roads a new colour | Stop people from moving | *Change the way travel works
test: Ella ___ the wet clay into a little owl. Which word fits? | barely | curt | travelled | *reshaped
exam: Which meaning fits «reshape the future»? | To forget what happened in the past | To wait patiently for the future to arrive | *To change what the future will be like | To draw a picture of tomorrow
